{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed Phase 1 RCA before repair.\n\nMechanism: `attach_commits` resolves ticket storage independently, but then passes that tracker path to `commit_impact.unresolvable_shas`; `code_root_for` defines the code repository as `dirname(tracker)`. With an absolute relocated store, valid code SHAs are therefore checked by `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse` instead of against the caller/current code checkout (`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:255,269`; `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py:135-147`).\n\nRuntime proof in disposable separate code/store trees: the unchanged CLI command rejected valid `HEAD`; instrumentation captured `git -C /tmp/rebar-attach-rca-9918.Xt20YN/external rev-parse ... HEAD^{commit}`. Direct A/B validation returned `[]` at the code root and `[HEAD]` at the tracker parent. Even `rebar.attach_commits(..., repo_root=<code-root>)` still traced the tracker parent and failed, rejecting the CLI-omission rival. Monkeypatching only `code_root_for` to the code checkout made the valid attachment record a COMMITS event while a bogus SHA remained rejected, ruling out ticket lookup, append, Git, and all-or-nothing validation failures. A default in-repo tracker control continued to succeed.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. Relocated stores are explicitly supported (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:64-67`, `docs/config.md:208-212`), while the attach contract requires each SHA to resolve in the repository (`src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md:54-71`).\n\nCaller gate: only `_lib_mutations.attach_commits` calls the tracker-derived helpers. CLI, library, and MCP converge on this seam, and no caller depends on tracker-parent validation. Expected post-fix behavior: code SHA validation uses explicit `repo_root`, then `REBAR_ROOT`, then the cwd Git top-level, while tracker reads/writes continue through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`; genuinely unknown SHAs remain all-or-nothing failures."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787044279580268001,"uuid":"c40489dd-9442-4486-9067-bdc54afd51cc"}